// Title: Insecure Proxy/DOH Transfer Via Curl.EXE
// Sigma ID: 2c1486f5-02e8-4f86-9099-b97f2da4ed77
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-07-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects execution of "curl.exe" with the "insecure" flag over proxy or DOH.
// False positives:
//   - Access to badly maintained internal or development systems
// References:
//   - https://curl.se/docs/manpage.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_curl_insecure_proxy_or_doh.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\curl.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "curl.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--doh-insecure" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--proxy-insecure")
